This is a real bug, which I just found; the fix will probably be in patchlevel
3.  The problem is in the routine explmm in mhitm.c, which will damage you
as well as the main victim if the explosion happens next to you.  The
problem is that when it tries to damage you, it doesn't know that the
"damage" is blinding damage and so it tries to do hit point damage instead.
